' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's own native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention.
'
' Array.SortBy/MinBy/MaxBy -- real CALLABLE support (see
' fission/tests/native_programs/callables.abas's own header comment for
' the general ADDRESSOF/callable design this builds on). Each calls the
' user's own key function back once per array element, a genuine
' dispatch through the SAME closed-candidate-set `str_equals` chain
' `callables.abas` already exercises, hand-emitted as real INLINE native
' codegen directly in the caller's own function body (a plain host C
' function has no way to call back into ArcoBASIC-compiled code at all).
'
' Exercises: SortBy ascending/descending with a Number key on a Number
' array, SortBy with a Number key on a String array (also exercises the
' real `LEN(string)` fix this same pass found and closed -- a
' previously-missing case since bare LEN only ever supported arrays
' before), MinBy/MaxBy on both; a real STABILITY check (many elements
' sharing the SAME key must keep their original relative order, matching
' the oracle's own real `std::stable_sort`); a callable variable
' reassigned to a DIFFERENT key function between two SortBy calls; a
' void SortBy call (result discarded); SortBy on a genuinely empty array
' (a real, safe, disclosed simplification -- no crash, an empty result).
'
' Number and String key kinds only (a real, disclosed, narrower scope,
' matching the established Array.Sort/Find/Contains precedent) -- not
' exercised here since every fixture in this file already stays within
' that supported subset.
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
FUNCTION Negate(x)
    RETURN 0 - x
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION StrLen(s)
    RETURN LEN(s)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Parity(x)
    RETURN x MOD 2
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Zero(x)
    RETURN 0
END FUNCTION

nums = [5, 1, 4, 2, 3]
PRINT Array.SortBy(nums, ADDRESSOF Negate)
PRINT Array.SortBy(nums, ADDRESSOF Negate, TRUE)
PRINT nums

words = ["banana", "kiwi", "fig", "apple"]
PRINT Array.SortBy(words, ADDRESSOF StrLen)

PRINT Array.MinBy(nums, ADDRESSOF Negate)
PRINT Array.MaxBy(nums, ADDRESSOF Negate)
PRINT Array.MinBy(words, ADDRESSOF StrLen)
PRINT Array.MaxBy(words, ADDRESSOF StrLen)

vals = [10, 21, 32, 43, 54, 65]
PRINT Array.SortBy(vals, ADDRESSOF Parity)

f = ADDRESSOF Parity
PRINT Array.SortBy(vals, f)
f = ADDRESSOF Zero
PRINT Array.SortBy(vals, f)

ignored = Array.SortBy(vals, ADDRESSOF Parity)

e = Array.New(0, 0)
PRINT Array.SortBy(e, ADDRESSOF Negate)
PRINT LEN(Array.SortBy(e, ADDRESSOF Negate))
